-- title:
--   Minimal number of generators of the kernel of a surjection of regular local rings
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings, each assumed to be a regular local ring, and let $f \colon A \to B$ be a surjective ring homomorphism. The assertion is the equality
--   $$\mu(\ker f) + \dim B = \dim A$$
--   of elements of $\mathrm{WithBot}\,\mathbb{N}_\infty$, the value monoid of `ringKrullDim`. Here $\dim$ denotes the Krull dimension of a commutative ring, $\ker f$ is the kernel ideal of $f$ viewed as an $A$-submodule of $A$, and $\mu(\ker f)$ is its `spanFinrank`, namely the natural number obtained from the minimal cardinality of a generating set of the ideal $\ker f$ (finite here, since a regular local ring is noetherian), coerced into $\mathrm{WithBot}\,\mathbb{N}_\infty$. Equivalently: the kernel of a surjection of regular local rings needs exactly $\dim A - \dim B$ generators, and in particular the Krull dimensions of $A$ and $B$, which are finite, differ by that minimal number of generators. The proof cites the fact that a regular local ring is a domain.
--
--   This is the quantitative form of the classical criterion that a quotient of a regular local ring $A$ is again regular precisely when the kernel is generated by part of a regular system of parameters, so that the kernel requires exactly $\dim A - \dim B$ generators. It is used in the construction of the relative group law on Jacobians of curves with good reduction, in the lemmas producing open neighbourhoods on which the difference map along the diagonal extends.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_spanFinrank_ker_add_ringKrullDim_eq.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open IsLocalRing

theorem IsRegularLocalRing.spanFinrank_ker_add_ringKrullDim_eq
    {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsRegularLocalRing A] [IsRegularLocalRing B]
    (f : A →+* B) (hf : Function.Surjective f) :
    ((RingHom.ker f).spanFinrank : WithBot ℕ∞) + ringKrullDim B = ringKrullDim A := by sorry
